---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Beat from '../components/Beat.astro';
import Steps from '../components/Steps.astro';
import IfThen from '../components/IfThen.astro';
import Stats from '../components/Stats.astro';
---

<Base
  audience="investors"
  title="For investors"
  description="A platform that connects landlords who plan to sell with tenants who want to buy."
  noindex
>
  <Beat label="For investors">
    <h1 class="say">Millions of renters want to buy. Thousands of landlords want to sell.</h1>
    <p class="say">
      <span class="hl">Often, they already share a front door.</span>
    </p>
  </Beat>

  <Beat label="The opportunity">
    <Stats
      items={[
        { n: '58%', l: 'of private renters in England expect to buy a home' },
        { n: '4.1%', l: 'actually buy each year' },
        { n: '31%', l: 'of landlords plan to sell some or all homes within two years' },
        { n: '42 of 74', l: "lenders accept a landlord's discount to a sitting tenant" },
      ]}
    />
    <p class="after">
      Since 1 May 2026, landlords can no longer end tenancies without a reason, and a landlord who
      evicts to sell cannot re-let for a year. Selling to the tenant is becoming the easier exit.
    </p>
  </Beat>

  <Beat label="What we are building">
    <p class="mid">
      A platform that connects landlords who plan to sell with tenants who want to buy, and turns
      rent already being paid into a discount on the home.
    </p>
    <ul class="lines">
      <li>We own no homes and hold no customers' money.</li>
      <li>The tenant pays nothing beyond market rent.</li>
      <li>The landlord pays us, and still comes out ahead of using agents.</li>
      <li>The sale uses a lending route that already exists, the concessionary purchase.</li>
    </ul>
  </Beat>

  <Beat label="How we earn">
    <IfThen
      rows={[
        { if: 'Tenant-finding fee', then: '£500 per letting, paid by the landlord.' },
        { if: 'Ledger fee', then: '1.5% of rent collected, for keeping the credit record.' },
        { if: 'Sale fee', then: '1% of the price when a tenant buys.' },
        {
          if: 'Mortgage introductions',
          then: 'Possible later, if confirmed as permitted. Not in our numbers.',
        },
      ]}
    />
    <p class="after">
      About £740 per home per year on a London reference home, assuming one in five tenants buy
      within five years.
    </p>
  </Beat>

  <Beat label="The numbers, honestly">
    <div class="tbl">
      <table>
        <caption class="sr-only">
          Yearly income by number of homes and share of tenants who buy
        </caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Homes on the platform</th>
            <th scope="col" class="r">
              If 10% buy
            </th>
            <th scope="col" class="r">
              If 20% buy
            </th>
            <th scope="col" class="r">
              If 30% buy
            </th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">50</th>
            <td class="r">£32,000</td>
            <td class="r">£37,000</td>
            <td class="r">£42,000</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">300</th>
            <td class="r">£190,000</td>
            <td class="r">£221,000</td>
            <td class="r">£253,000</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">1,000</th>
            <td class="r">£632,000</td>
            <td class="r">£738,000</td>
            <td class="r">£843,000</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="after">
      Yearly income once homes have been listed long enough for sales. No sale can happen in a
      home's first 12 months.
    </p>
    <Stats
      items={[
        { n: '~£340k', l: 'estimated funding to reach the end of year two' },
        { n: '350–500', l: 'homes needed to break even, on our estimates' },
      ]}
    />
    <p class="after">
      Costs are our estimates and have not yet been quoted. The share of tenants who buy is unknown
      until the pilot measures it.
    </p>
  </Beat>

  <Beat label="The plan">
    <Steps
      steps={[
        {
          when: 'Now',
          what: "Legal opinion and an approach to the FCA's Innovation Pathways service.",
        },
        { when: 'Pilot', what: '25 to 50 homes with landlords who already use agents.' },
        { when: 'Month 12', what: 'First tenants become able to buy. We measure who does.' },
        { when: 'Year two', what: 'Around 300 homes.' },
        {
          when: 'Later',
          what: 'An investor fund joins as a landlord, buying new homes in bulk under an independent authorised manager.',
        },
      ]}
    />
  </Beat>

  <Beat label="What could go wrong">
    <IfThen
      rows={[
        {
          if: 'Few tenants can afford to buy',
          then: 'The credit is a few per cent of the price. We select tenants with a realistic plan and start in more affordable areas.',
        },
        {
          if: 'Lenders value homes lower',
          then: 'The discount can shrink or disappear. An independent valuation comes first.',
        },
        {
          if: 'Income per home is thin',
          then: 'About £740 a year. Costs must stay low until scale.',
        },
        {
          if: 'Our reading of the rules is wrong',
          then: 'We will not launch before a legal opinion.',
        },
        {
          if: 'House prices fall',
          then: 'We own no homes. Landlords may delay sales, which slows our sale fees.',
        },
      ]}
    />
  </Beat>

  <Beat label="Next step">
    <p class="mid">
      If this fits what you look for, ask the person who shared this page for a conversation and the
      full business plan.
    </p>
    <p class="notice">
      This page is information for experienced investors, not an offer or invitation to invest. Any
      investment would be made only on separate documents and after taking your own advice. All
      figures are estimates and may not be achieved.
    </p>
  </Beat>
</Base>
